---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { consentConfig } from '../../config';
import { routePath } from '../../i18n';

const months = Math.round(consentConfig.maxAgeDays / 30);
---
<LegalLayout title="Cookie policy" description="Which storage and analytics technologies greibersalas.com uses and how to manage them.">
  <p><em>This is a translation provided for convenience. In case of discrepancy, the <a href={routePath('cookies', 'es')} hreflang="es">Spanish version</a> prevails.</em></p>

  <h2>1. What are cookies?</h2>
  <p>Cookies and similar technologies (such as the browser's local storage) store or read information on your device. Article 22.2 of the Spanish LSSI-CE requires informing you and asking for consent, except for strictly necessary ones.</p>

  <h2>2. What does this site use?</h2>
  <p><strong>This site does not set its own or third-party cookies.</strong> It only uses:</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th><th>Consent</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>{consentConfig.storageKey}</code></td>
          <td>Local storage (first-party)</td>
          <td>Remember your privacy choice.</td>
          <td>{months} months</td>
          <td>Not required (technical)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Umami (cloud.umami.is)</td>
          <td>Cookie-free analytics (third-party)</td>
          <td>Anonymous, aggregated statistics of visits and clicks on contact buttons.</td>
          <td>Stores nothing on your device</td>
          <td>Yes — only loaded if you accept</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>3. Linked external services</h2>
  <p>Links to LinkedIn and WhatsApp take you to third-party services. Their own privacy and cookie policies apply when you open them; this site doesn't load any content from those services.</p>

  <h2>4. How to manage your choice</h2>
  <p>You can accept, reject or change your choice at any time from <button type="button" class="inline-link" data-cc-open>Cookie settings</button> (also available in the footer). Your choice is renewed every {months} months. You can also clear local storage from your browser settings.</p>
  <p>More information on data processing in the <a href={routePath('privacy', 'en')}>privacy policy</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
